Live draw: a colour texture whose offset lies inside a live colour surface (not at its base) samples that rectangle of the
surface instead of stale guest VRAM. ToD's post chain resolves the scene into the display buffer (0:0x0 / 0:0x438000, a
1280x704 surface, pitch 5120) and samples it as a 1280x704 A8R8G8B8 texture at row 8 (0xA000 / 0x442000) for its bloom
downsample and four screen-space sprites (tods-ng-b1 draws.csv). The surface lookup matched base offsets only, so those reads
took never-written VRAM. Same pitch, same format family (A8R8G8B8 read of an RGBA8 surface), clipped to the surface, recopied
when the surface's colour generation changes; 8 cached windows with their own SRV slots after the RG16 range.
LD_CWIN=0 = old behaviour. Upstream candidate (general: any title sampling a sub-rectangle of a render target).

